Keeps this directory in git, which is load-bearing rather than tidy.

The Dockerfile copies apps/web/public into the runtime image. Git does not track
empty directories, so without a file here a fresh clone has no public/ at all and
`docker build` fails on that COPY with "failed to compute cache key ... not found"
-- a message that names the layer rather than the cause. The repo built fine on
any machine that had ever run the app, and failed on every clean checkout.

Delete this once there is a favicon to replace it (ROADMAP, Loose ends).
